WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:10.690
(Music)

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.193
Emily has a wild imagination.

00:00:13.193 --> 00:00:16.279
Bee, I was hoping you'd come.

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:17.656
What's up?

00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:18.949
(Music)

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.869
Alena Smith:
She's always asking for someone
to understand her.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:26.456
And it feels like she becomes
increasing alone.

00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:29.376
Alena Smith:
But because she's Emily, she's
conducting all sorts of 

00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:31.378
Alena Smith:
relationships with imaginary
figures.

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:33.630
How did you get inside?

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.757
Girl, I flew through the window.

00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:38.802
Hailee Steinfeld:
The Bee is a figment of Emily's
imagination.

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:43.515
The Bee shows up every time
Emily was feeling a bit lost, or
alone.

00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:45.183
Will you dance with me?

00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:48.144
Hailee Steinfeld:
And the bumblebee will sort of
come in and save the day.

00:00:48.144 --> 00:00:49.688
Bee, you're so sweet.

00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:51.982
I'm covered in pollen, baby.

00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:53.108
Emily:
Bee!

00:00:53.108 --> 00:00:55.652
Alena Smith:
The show explores that being
alone,

00:00:55.652 --> 00:00:59.239
Alena Smith:
can be tough, but perhaps that
was the very thing 

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:02.075
that generated such
powerful creativity.

00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:03.493
May I have this dance?

00:01:03.493 --> 00:01:05.328
Bee, you don't mind, do you?

00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:06.788
(Music)

00:01:06.788 --> 00:01:08.248
Buzz...

00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:12.252
(Music)

